# Incident write-up template

## Summary
One or two sentences: what broke, who was affected, how long.

## Timeline (all times in one time zone)
| Time | Event |
|---|---|
| hh:mm | First report |
| hh:mm | Incident declared |
| hh:mm | Root cause identified |
| hh:mm | Fix applied |
| hh:mm | Service confirmed healthy |

## Impact
Users, sites and systems affected. Numbers where you have them.

## Hypothesis log
| Hypothesis | Evidence for | Evidence against | Status |
|---|---|---|---|

## Root cause
What actually happened, in plain language.

## Fix
What was changed, by whom, and how it was checked.

## Follow-ups
Owner and date for each preventive action.

## Short fictional example
A software update was pushed to several hundred machines in two waves.
The machines bypassed the local cache server and all downloaded through
the shared proxy, which saturated and slowed web access at multiple
sites. The incident was declared at 14:27 and the root cause confirmed
at 15:16. Follow-up: route updates through the cache server and stagger
future waves.
